From: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 03:02:47 +0200
Subject: Accept a second 1.09 build of Diablo's DIABDAT.MPQ

gdp knew one DIABDAT.MPQ, GOG's (517501282 bytes, inside its installer). A player's own
1.09 copy is 517501242 bytes, 40 bytes smaller, and was refused. DIABDAT.MPQ is now a
placeholder for two alternatives, GOG's (DIABDAT.MPQ?gog, still provided by the installer)
and the new one (DIABDAT.MPQ?1.09) with its size, md5, sha1 and sha256, as hexen.wad does,
so diablo-data is built from either.

Forwarded: not yet (candidate for Debian)

diff --git a/data/diablo.yaml b/data/diablo.yaml
--- a/data/diablo.yaml
+++ b/data/diablo.yaml
@@ -21,11 +21,17 @@ packages:
       - hellfire mpq
 
 files:
+  DIABDAT.MPQ:
+    alternatives:
+      - DIABDAT.MPQ?gog
+      # Walnut: another 1.09 DIABDAT.MPQ build, 40 bytes smaller than GOG's
+      - DIABDAT.MPQ?1.09
+
   setup_diablo_1.09_hellfire_v4_(78466).exe:
     unpack:
       format: innoextract
     provides:
-      - DIABDAT.MPQ
+      - DIABDAT.MPQ?gog
       - hellfire mpq
       - gog pdf
       - Readme.txt
@@ -34,7 +40,8 @@ groups:
